# Build target for esbuild (via @angular/build).
#
# Without this, @angular/build falls back to a default browser set that predates
# ES2018 object spread, so esbuild lowers `{ ...a, ...b }` and injects the
# TypeScript-style helpers `__spreadValues` / `__spreadProps`.
#
# That is fatal for mapbox-gl: the dev build code-splits it into its own chunk,
# the helper definition lands in a *different* chunk, and the mapbox chunk ends
# up with 131 unresolved `__spreadValues` references. mapbox also runs this code
# inside a Blob worker, which has no access to the other chunk's scope, so the
# tile pipeline dies with:
#   ReferenceError: __spreadValues is not defined
# and the coverage map renders blank with no visible error.
#
# Production builds only survive by accident: minification renames and inlines
# the helpers, so the bug never appears outside `ng serve`.
